          site should say, you can get something decent up on your own.
        </p>
        <p data-wd-reveal="up">
          But making the page was never the hard part. It’s buying the domain and pointing it at
          the right place. The certificate. The contact form that actually sends somewhere you’ll
          see it. Claiming and verifying your Google listing. Getting indexed. Most DIY sites end
          their lives as a nice page in a browser tab that never quite goes live.
        </p>
        <p data-wd-reveal="up">
          And I use these tools too. That’s part of why I’m not charging agency prices.
        </p>
        <div class="awkward__grid">
          <p class="awkward__punch" data-wd-reveal="pop">
